Omission
- [N1] Omitted trace (input 1): i1:To start the process for ACME, begin with the New Resupply Cycle -> i2:Check Levels of Inventory -> i3:If the inventory is below or equal to the minimum, generate an Equal to or below minimum Report. -> i5:create Purchase Orders (POs) -> i9:If the PO is created, it needs to be reviewed. -> i7:If the PO is rejected, it needs to be reworked. -> i5:create Purchase Orders (POs)
- [N2] Omitted trace (input 3): i1:To start the process for ACME, begin with the New Resupply Cycle -> i2:Check Levels of Inventory -> i3:If the inventory is below or equal to the minimum, generate an Equal to or below minimum Report. -> i5:create Purchase Orders (POs) -> i9:If the PO is created, it needs to be reviewed. -> i8:If the PO is approved, it is printed and released in the system. -> i10:Simultaneously, reserve funds for the released POs and mail the POs to the supplier. -> i13:If the POs are mailed to the supplier, receive the inventory. -> i15:If the inventory is received, proceed to receive the Packing Slip. -> i14:If the Packing Slip is received, proceed to receive the Invoice. -> i16:If the Invoice is received, proceed to the Three-way match. -> i17:If the Three-way match is successful, release the funds. -> i18:Once the funds are released, issue the payment. -> i19:After the payment is issued, the Resupply Cycle is complete and the process ends.
- [N3] Within matched traces (2->0) omitted: i11:If funds are reserved for the released POs, receive the Packing Slip.

